# Engineering Workflow

For every non-trivial task:

1. Inspect the repository before proposing changes.
2. Identify the project stack and existing conventions.
3. Create a short implementation plan.
4. Delegate implementation to a stack specialist when that materially improves quality.
   Do not delegate small edits that touch only one or two files—the main agent should implement those.
   Do not delegate architect, security-reviewer, qa-tester, code-reviewer, or production-code-review unless the user explicitly asks.
5. Use an implementation skill when it matches the task.
   Do not apply production-code-review unless the user invokes it.
6. Keep changes scoped to the requested task.
7. Do not run the test suite, a code review, or the production checklist as part of every task.
8. Ask before destructive operations, dependency upgrades,
   database changes or production deployments.

Do not invent API contracts, environment variables or business rules.

For financial, banking, payment or authentication work, enable the project's fintech-security rule when present.
